{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== SESSION SEGMENT: hardening epic 9227 + epic 061c tail. Handoff state below. ===\n\nCLOSED THIS SEGMENT (7): 7761, 172e, 343b, 7cbe, b00f, d8ef, b300.\nIN REVIEW: b5fe (change 1160, awaiting both votes). 18 Gerrit changes open, 17 SUBMITTABLE.\nNEXT ON THE CRITICAL PATH: d23e (review running) -> eb58 closes -> unblocks S6 0d76 / S8 eb6e /\nS9 8625 -> 3768 -> 5e75 -> epic closes -> land the stack.\n\nWHAT WAS BUILT\n 7761  Pass-1 ladder expressed in model classes. The back-compat rule is load-bearing: resolve_class\n       PREFIXES the inferred provider, so an unconditional resolve hands callers\n       anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 where they have always seen the bare name. Each rung compares its\n       class resolution against its own inferred form and keeps the bare name when they match.\n 172e  Code review's Pass-2 verify step now declares `model: standard`. This also fixed a SECOND\n       defect nobody had noticed: the step's `temperature: 0` had NEVER taken effect, because\n       pydantic-ai's Anthropic adapter drops temperature on the frontier model. Code review has never\n       had the greedy determinism its config claims until now.\n 343b  provider_provenance reaches production verdicts. The gap was that every prior test handed\n       build_payload a verdict that ALREADY contained the key — a constructed-input pass proving the\n       persist step and never the path.\n 7cbe  The global pipx rebar was two weeks stale and SILENTLY disabling the plan-review LLM tier. TWO\n       causes: a stale uv 0.7.18 at ~/.local/bin shadowing homebrew's 0.12.0 on the updater's PATH,\n       and the pipx venv PINNED to backend=pip (pipx ignores --backend uv for an existing venv).\n       Fixed by PATH precedence + recreating the venv. Verified UNDER LAUNCHD, which is the only\n       proof that matters: by-hand runs inherit a rich shell env, launchd supplies a minimal one.\n 9227  New epic: preemptive hardening of low-headroom high-centrality modules. b00f (env-registry\n       _llm_float, 4 undocumented env vars), d8ef (seam guards), b300 (config.py 793->631 via\n       gate_context.py), b5fe (workflow_ops.py 794->511 via decide_ops.py).\n\nMEASURED HEADROOM WON: config.py 793 -> 631. workflow_ops.py 794 -> 511. runner.py already 647 from\nADR 0056. STILL AT EXACTLY 800 AND UNTICKETED: plan_review/passes.py, _engine/rebar_reconciler/\noutbound_differ.py. attest.py is ticket c6c9. signing.py 798.\n\nOPERATOR DECISIONS RECORDED\n * The per-FUNCTION length ratchet is REJECTED (blast radius: 62 functions over 120 lines across six\n   subsystems; epic 716f removed the allowlist). Seam tests are the substitute ratchet and are\n   therefore load-bearing, not decorative. DO NOT re-propose the ratchet.\n * 1132's LLM-Review was restored by the operator; the stack is unblocked.\n\nTRAPS THAT COST REAL TIME — READ BEFORE PLANNING ANYTHING\n 1. AN AC WHOSE EVIDENCE IS A COMMIT MESSAGE OR A TICKET COMMENT IS STRUCTURALLY UNCONFIRMABLE. The\n    completion verifier reads REPOSITORY FILES ONLY and cannot read git history. This appeared on\n    FOUR tickets (7cbe, b300, b5fe, 5e75) because \"record why you did this\" is the natural phrasing.\n    Always split: the durable half goes in a docstring or a test, the narrative half gets\n    [operator-attested].\n 2. A PLAN THAT NARRATES TRANSIENT STATE IS FALSIFIED BY ITS OWN SIBLINGS. Twice: b300's AC2 said\n    config.py \"has no such guard today\" (d8ef was about to add one) and b5fe's AC2 said the seam test\n    \"currently loops against ONE shared bound\" (b300 split it first). Write the required END STATE.\n 3. NEVER EDIT A TICKET'S MATERIAL WHILE A REVIEW OF IT OR ITS PARENT IS IN FLIGHT, and never once\n    signed unless you mean to pay for a re-review. Editing child d8ef mid-review made 9227's first\n    sign fail with stale-pin-drift. Comments are NOT material and are always safe.\n 4. AN UNSCOPED ATTESTATION (no file_impact) DIES ON EVERY COMMIT with stale-head. 9227 was unscoped\n    and died on its first child commit. Set file_impact BEFORE reviewing — after is a material edit.\n 5. PROCESS-GLOBAL STATE MAKES A GUARD ORDER-DEPENDENT. d8ef's registry guard needs a SUBPROCESS: the\n    masking path is that tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites_heldout.py:11 imports\n    prerequisite_workflow_ops DIRECTLY, registering the op whether or not the production import\n    survives. Measured: in-process alone FAILS, in-process after that module PASSES, subprocess FAILS\n    correctly. NOTE the review's stated mechanism (module caching of workflow.steps) was WRONG; the\n    conclusion was right. d23e's \"warning fires once per process\" AC has the same shape.\n 6. THE ENV-REGISTRY GATE FIRES ON ANY LINE-COUNT CHANGE to a file containing a non-literal env read.\n    config.py is such a file. Run `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py` and commit docs/env-vars.md.\n 7. DO NOT RUN THE FULL SUITE CONCURRENTLY WITH COMMITS in the same worktree: tests/conftest.py:448's\n    HEAD-movement guard misreports your own commits as test-created and its remedy text advises\n    `git reset --hard`, which would destroy real work.\n 8. ADR 0056's declarative-field-table prescription for config.py is NOT VIABLE. gen_env_registry.py\n    records a read only when the env name is a STRING LITERAL, so a spec-row table makes 19 rows\n    vanish and fails CI. The repo already tried and rejected that shape (model_classes.py:112-130).\n\nMETHOD THAT WORKED, and is worth continuing\n * PRE-EMPTIVE AC READS. Reading each ticket's criteria as the reviewer would — not with a keyword\n   scan — caught defects on b5fe (3), d23e (4), 3768 (2) and 5e75 (2) before any review round. One\n   was a cross-ticket hazard no gate would have found until CI went red naming the wrong file.\n * SWEEP THE CLASS, not the cited instance. d8ef cost five rounds largely because each round fixed\n   only what was named.\n * VERIFY BEFORE ASSERTING. A \"circular dependency\" on d23e evaporated on inspection\n   (infra/runbooks/ already exists with ten files). A claim that plan_review_recovery.py:8's docstring\n   was stale was FALSE — it is accurate; the stale text is test_gate_dispatch_seam.py's assertion\n   message. Both were caught by reading the cited line.\n * HELD-OUT TDD, every code leaf. Implementers passed the held-out sets on b300 (5 unseen) and b5fe\n   (4 unseen). Mutations bit every time EXCEPT one, recorded honestly: dropping decide_ops'\n   registration import did NOT fail, because the re-export already imports the module — the mutation\n   was not a defect, the guard is sound."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785582392149317001,"uuid":"a73495f7-54fa-44d7-8971-7c9974eb9a7f"}